From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:38:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] vdin: stamp each v4l2 buffer when its frame completes

The capture queue declared copied timestamps, which a capture driver has
nobody to copy from, so every buffer reached the client with time 0. A
client could not tell how old a frame was or whether frames were lost.
---
 drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c b/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c
--- a/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c
+++ b/drivers/media/vin/tvin/vdin/vdin_v4l2_if.c
@@ -0,6 +0,7 @@
 	list_del(&devp->cur_buff->list);
 	spin_unlock(&devp->list_head_lock);
 	devp->vdin_v4l2.stats.done_cnt++;
+	vb2buf->timestamp = ktime_get_ns();
 	vb2_buffer_done(vb2buf, VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -0,7 +0,7 @@
 	/*que->mem_ops = &vb2_vmalloc_memops;*/
 	/*que->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_sg_memops;*/
 
-	que->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_COPY;
+	que->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC | V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TSTAMP_SRC_EOF;
 	/*
 	 * Assume that this DMA engine needs to have at least two buffers
 	 * available before it can be started. The start_streaming() op
